H1567.strongs:
Origin: from 1530 and 5707; heap of testimony;
Meaning: Galed, a memorial cairn East of the Jordan
KJV renders: Galeed.

H1568.strongs:
Origin: probably from 1567;
Meaning: Gilad, a region East of the Jordan; also the name of three Israelites
KJV renders: Gilead, Gileadite.

H1569.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 1568;
Meaning: a Giladite or descendant of Gilad
KJV renders: Gileadite.

H1570.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: probably to caper (as a goat)
KJV renders: appear.

H1571.strongs:
Origin: by contraction from an unused root meaning to gather;
Meaning: properly, assemblage; used only adverbially also, even, yea, though; often repeated as correl. both...and
KJV renders: again, alike, also, (so much) as (soon), both (so)...and, but, either...or, even, for all, (in) likewise (manner), moreover, nay...neither, one, then(-refore), though, what, with, yea.

H1573.strongs:
Origin: from 1572;
Meaning: properly, an absorbent, i.e. the bulrush (from its porosity); specifically the papyrus
KJV renders: (bul-) rush.

H1574.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root apparently meaning to grasp;
Meaning: properly, a span
KJV renders: cubit.

H1575.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 1574;
Meaning: a warrior (as grasping weapons)
KJV renders: Gammadims.

H1576.strongs:
Origin: from 1580;
Meaning: treatment, i.e. an act (of good or ill); by implication, service or requital
KJV renders: as hast served, benefit, desert, deserving, that which he hath given, recompense, reward.

H1577.strongs:
Origin: passive participle of 1580; rewarded;
Meaning: Gamul, an Israelite
KJV renders: Gamul. See also 1014.

H1578.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 1576;
Meaning: meaning the same
KJV renders: deed, recompense, such a reward.

H1579.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Gimzo, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Gimzo.

H1580.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to treat a person (well or ill), i.e. benefit or requite; by implication (of toil), to ripen, i.e. (specifically) to wean
KJV renders: bestow on, deal bountifully, do (good), recompense, requite, reward, ripen, serve, mean, yield.

H1581.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 1580 (in the sense of labor or burden-bearing);
Meaning: a camel
KJV renders: camel.

H1582.strongs:
Origin: probably from 1581; cameldriver;
Meaning: Gemalli, an Israelite
KJV renders: Gemalli.

H1583.strongs:
Origin: from 1580 and 410; reward of God;
Meaning: Gamliel, an Israelite
KJV renders: Gamaliel.

H1584.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to end (in the sense of completion or failure)
KJV renders: cease, come to an end, fail, perfect, perform.

H1586.strongs:
Origin: from 1584; completion;
Meaning: Gomer, the name of a son of Japheth and of his descendants; also of a Hebrewess
KJV renders: Gomer.

H1587.strongs:
Origin: or גְּמַרְיָהוּ; from 1584 and 3050; Jah has perfected;
Meaning: Gemarjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Gemariah.

H1588.strongs:
Origin: from 1598;
Meaning: a garden (as fenced)
KJV renders: garden.

H1589.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to thieve (literally or figuratively); by implication, to deceive
KJV renders: carry away, × indeed, secretly bring, steal (away), get by stealth.

H1590.strongs:
Origin: from 1589;
Meaning: a stealer
KJV renders: thief.

H1591.strongs:
Origin: from 1589;
Meaning: stealing, i.e. (concretely) something stolen
KJV renders: theft.

H1592.strongs:
Origin: from 1589; theft;
Meaning: Genubath, an Edomitish prince
KJV renders: Genubath.

H1593.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 1588;
Meaning: a garden
KJV renders: garden.

H1595.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to store;
Meaning: treasure; by implication, a coffer
KJV renders: chest, treasury.

H1596.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 1595;
Meaning: treasure
KJV renders: treasure.

H1597.strongs:
Origin: prolonged from 1595;
Meaning: a treasury
KJV renders: treasury.

H1598.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to hedge about, i.e. (generally) protect
KJV renders: defend.

H1599.strongs:
Origin: or גִּנְּתוֹ; from 1598; gardener;
Meaning: Ginnethon or Ginnetho, an Israelite
KJV renders: Ginnetho, Ginnethon.
